\section{Background}

We have defined and demonstrated a model to detect plagiarism from text sources with significant changes made. This task differs significantly from traditional text comparison tasks like summarization or sentiment classification. The plagiarism detection task requires us to capture and generate new text which is likely to exist only in one of the documents. To achieve this, we developed a hybrid model to capture both the semantic and syntactic relationships between sentences in order to capture the essential meaning of a text. 

